hi there steve kaufman  we are now approaching  or starting  week 4 of this 12-week course  this 12-week  concentrated effort to achieve a  breakthrough in the language and i have  spoken about the importance of doing  something every day  the importance of varying your  activities the fundamental importance of  listening because listening  comprehension  is to my mind the most important skill  with good listening comprehension you  read better  you get to speak better so you need to  do a lot of listening and listening is  easy to fit into your schedule but today  i want to talk about  linking linking is sort of the unique  function at link lingq link when we say  linking we mean creating links we mean  if you're on your ipad with a stylus  you know pointing out a word or clicking  on a word  in order to see first of all what it  means now remember  the meaning of the word we call it a  hint because a word can have different  meanings in different contexts the  dictionary definition sometimes is not  relevant to the text that you are  looking at  and so that this hint is sort of a start  it helps you  you know  start the process of getting a sense of  what a word means how it's used with  which other words what's the full scope  of the meaning and when you look a word  up don't uh you know  in depending on the language you're  learning  uh  and  your you know your native language there  are a variety of dictionaries that you  can hook up to at link  so  choose one that you like and i tend to  use several different dictionaries  because  they provide different services if you  want sometimes i just use hints that  other people have chosen don't forget we  cash  we store  hints that other people have selected so  that you needn't go to the dictionary  but sometimes that's not the hint or the  meaning that you want for a particular  context and so very often i go to other  dictionaries  and dictionaries can sometimes have  different interpretations of words so  it's useful to look at different  dictionaries and i tend to rely on those  dictionaries that i find the best  and  you know  very often in say romance languages  where you know  verb endings tenses or  declensions in slavic languages  are things that causes difficulty and so  then there are some dictionaries that  are better than others at showing us  uh you know for example context reverso  is very good in this regard so you'll  see the verb you'll see where it fits in  you'll see what the conjugation is so i  like to have these different resources  that i can use when i you know create a  link and look up a word  uh you can tag  your links  you can look up sort of the grammatical  sometimes in some of the languages we  tell you this is a noun and then you can  look up  in our grammar resources how nouns or  verbs function in that language so there  are lots of bits of information you can  get when you create a link  now the next thing about creating links  is that you have now started or you've  added these to your database of words  and phrases so  uh  even though you won't remember the first  time you look up a word the next time  you see that word  which was blue  generally speaking when you created that  link it's not yellow it's now yellow and  it's a darker yellow and gradually moves  to a lighter and lighter shade of yellow  as you get a better and better sense of  the meaning of that word  once you've created a link you can now  review these links in flashcards  dictation  fill in the blanks multiple choice the  different activities that we have  and here again  i like to do this when i move from page  to page in  when i'm reading a lesson of link but  other people like to do it in the  vocabulary section uh using this based  repetition model that we have so there  are a variety of ways in which once  you've created these links you can then  review them and get a better handle on  on these and try to remember them  so and links also when you create links  not only is the number of links you  create an indication of your activity  level because you should be creating  links i create links even if i kind of  half know the meaning of the word i link  it  and sometimes  when i have moved a word to known  either because i manually did so  or i never saved it initially because i  thought i knew the meaning of the word  and then i'm not so confident anymore  any word that has already moved to white  you can link it again and just the  statistics adjust so my goal is to make  my my page at length lighter and lighter  in color blue becomes yellow yellow  becomes white but sometimes a word has  moved to white  uh  prematurely and then i just link it  again so i'm uh you know i don't  hesitate to create links and creating  links is an indication that you are  active and the more active you are  the faster you are going to learn and of  course creating links helps the system  guess  and what you know because words that you  don't link that you encounter blue words  that you encounter that you don't link  the system assumes that you know and so  you get this known words total gradually  drawing and again it's not scientific  ideally  uh like link will not save numbers so  that doesn't add to your known words  total and if it's a place name or a  personal name and you or a word in  another language  then you use the x  to ignore it or you can do that with  your cursor  and in that way it's not added to your  total but the known words total again is  a rough indicator of your progress in  the language it's a rough indicator of  your activity level it's not a  scientific number but it also depends on  you creating links so there are many  many reasons why you should be actively  creating links both of words and phrases  as a big part of your learning activity  so  starting on week four let's get out  there and create a lot of links

